## 📋 Overview  
The goal is to make the **Dashboard** the default landing page (`/`) of the application. The dashboard must contain three widget groups:

| Widget Group | Description | Data Source |
|--------------|-------------|-------------|
| **Summary Cards** | KPI‑style cards (e.g., Total Users, Active Sessions, Revenue) | `GET /api/dashboard/summary` |
| **Recent Activity** | Chronological list of the latest events (login, file upload, etc.) | `GET /api/dashboard/activity` |
| **Quick Actions** | Buttons / links for common tasks (Create Project, Invite User, Export Report) | Static config (can be extended via API) |

The layout must be **responsive** (mobile < 600 px, tablet 600‑900 px, desktop > 900 px) and integrate with the existing **App Drawer** navigation (so the drawer can still be opened/closed from the dashboard).

---

## 🛠️ Assumptions & Prerequisites  

| Item | Detail |
|------|--------|
| **Framework** | React 18 + React‑Router‑DOM v6 |
| **UI Library** | @mui/material (MUI v5) – already used in the project |
| **State Management** | React Query (tanstack/query) – already configured for data fetching |
| **API Base** | `import { apiClient } from '@/utils/apiClient'` (axios instance with auth interceptors) |
| **Testing** | Jest + React Testing Library (RTL) |
| **Styling** | MUI’s `sx` prop + theme breakpoints (no extra CSS files needed) |
| **Routing** | The app already has `<BrowserRouter>` wrapped around `<App />`. We will add a route for `/` that renders `<Dashboard />`. |

If any of the above differs in your repo, adjust the import paths accordingly.

---

## 📂 File‑by‑File Changes  

Below is a **complete, copy‑paste‑ready** set of modifications.  
All new files are created under `src/`. Existing files are only edited where indicated.

### 1. Routing – `src/App.tsx` (or `src/App.js`)

```diff
